    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Allen & Jacobs are delighted to present No.14 Albert Court East, Dublin 2. A beautifully restored 2bed/2 bath late Victorian Cottage to the Dublin rental market.This exceptional two-bedroom, two-bathroom home is discreetly tucked away on a quiet cul-de-sac in the heart of Dublin 2, just moments from the Grand Canal and Merrion Square. Extending to a generous standard of accommodation approximately 65sq.m, the property has been comprehensively renovated to create a superb contemporary home while carefully preserving its original period character.\n\nFinished to an exceptional standard throughout, the property enjoys a strong B3 BER rating and benefits from underfloor heating, upgraded insulation, double-glazed windows offering an excellent combination of comfort, efficiency and modern convenience.\nThe accommodation comprises a bright entrance hallway, two spacious double bedrooms with built-in wardrobes, a beautifully appointed principal en-suite, a contemporary main bathroom and a stunning open-plan kitchen, living and dining room extending across the full width of the property. \nThe bespoke fitted kitchen features integrated appliances, solid worktops and quality contemporary finishes, creating an ideal setting for comfortable day-to-day living. Sliding doors open onto a private south-facing patio garden providing ample natural light into the open plan living area while also creating a wonderfully private outdoor space ideal for relaxing or entertaining.\nAlbert Court enjoys an enviable location within one of Dublin`s most sought-after residential neighbourhoods. Grand Canal Dock, Merrion Square and the city centre are all within a short stroll, together with an outstanding selection of cafés, restaurants, bars and leisure amenities. The Bord Gáis Energy Theatre, Aviva Stadium and 3Arena are all nearby, while Grand Canal Dock DART Station provides excellent public transport links. Trinity College Dublin, Grafton Street, St. Stephen`s Green, Ballsbridge, Sandymount and the IFSC are all within comfortable walking distance.\nA rare opportunity to rent an exceptional period home in one of Dublin`s most desirable city locations.\n\nViewing\nStrictly by prior appointment only with sole agents\nAllen & Jacobs (City Centre Office)\n5 Bridge Street, Ringsend, Dublin 4\nTel: (01) 531 3939\nemail: lettings@allenandjacobs.ie\n"
      },
